; ============================================================================
;  KITCHEN  --  3.8 x 3.7 m, 2.4 m ceiling. Doorway on the -Z wall.
;
;  After the stairs and the bathroom, the kitchen is where the serious
;  domestic falls happen, and they have a particular shape: the fall is caused
;  by REACHING, not by walking.
;
;  Hazards
;    high shelf      everyday things stored above shoulder height. Reaching up
;                    and back shifts the centre of mass behind the heels --
;                    the classic kitchen fall, and the reason for the stool.
;    step stool      a light, wobbly stool with no handhold, left out because
;                    it is needed daily. Standing on it is worse than the
;                    reach it avoids.
;    wet floor       a spill by the sink on hard tile.
;    cupboard door   a low door left open across the walkway, at exactly shin
;                    height and below the natural line of sight.
;
;  The kettle is the decoy: an ordinary thing in an ordinary place.
; ============================================================================

